  "notes": [
    "Gallery r39 replaces group frames with independently measured pigment cutouts, common character/animal scales and one continuous surface-distance procession on each wall. All r38 art and unchanged TRELLIS geometry remain archived.",
    "Gallery r38 adds the helmeted Ryuichi-typeR among a mammoth, horse and aurochs on the existing deep west-wall bay, completing the shared 16-person contributor cast (nine Dots share one credit). Yuri remains a creator credit only. Geometry, earlier paintings and mascot availability are retained.",
    "Geometry r28-deep (user request 2026-10-14) remaps the same retained TRELLIS shell: the mouth and apron unchanged, the gallery uniformly lengthened by 7.9 m (x1.287) and the rounded rear chamber with its spring basin moved back 7.9 m along the bend, so one more 7.5 m procession fits on each wall. Topology, UVs and the embedded 1024 px textures are unchanged; model-r27-rounded.glb is kept.",
    "Gallery r37 paints @daredaro_F, a silver-haired gentleman whose eyes are hidden behind a bar, among a woolly rhinoceros, a reindeer and an ibex on the new east-wall bay; the upper animal register continues over the new bay on both walls.",
    "Geometry r27-rounded sculpts the retained TRELLIS shell into a rounded rear chamber and irregular shallow spring basin. The gallery through local Z=-29.5, all topology, UVs and 1024px textures are retained. Shared dim lighting, held torches and runtime water are identical in the waiting cave and live world. Earlier r26 files and immutable optimization records remain archived.",
    "The deep gallery keeps approximately 11 m width and 5.5 m centre headroom up to the back chamber. Existing measured source relief is expanded without moving the accepted mouth or replacing the cave with primitive geometry.",
    "Geometry r26 historical note: only its final 1.2 m rounded into a broad rear wall. The r27-rounded rear chamber now extends that same connected shell into a curved vault and spring basin.",
    "The measured aisle is 54.91 m, 2.11 times the original 26.00 m. The original outdoor campfire, river, mountain mesh and castle path are unchanged.",
    "White calcite wall albedo retains real rock relief, pores and bedding; pigments are projected directly onto those existing triangles. Warm fire illuminates the same faintly visible paintings.",
    "Gallery r30 restores the user-reference waving gray-white Rimo cat among two horses, an aurochs and a deer, directly opposite the unchanged west-wall 524. The cave geometry, walking surface and fire are unchanged.",
    "Gallery r31 includes all 13 released mascots among animal friezes. Cave placement is at ground level at the mountain foot near camp. Coming Soon is reserved for confirmed upcoming characters. The source cave GLB and earlier pigment files are retained.",
    "Gallery r32 integrates the faithful small 524 with a mammoth, two horses and an aurochs in one weathered transparent frieze, matching the opposite Rimo frieze. It replaces three separated west-wall placements. Earlier paintings and source models remain archived.",
    "Gallery r33 adds Maruimo among a bison, horse and deer. All 14 released mascots are represented; the Coming Soon reserve and original GLB remain unchanged.",
    "Gallery r34 adds two contributor processions on the west wall (Saber, Fairy, nukonuko, Saga; the Otani duck, Urata, Howkey). They replace the lone deer and bison, whose species reappear inside the friezes. The original GLB is unchanged.",
    "Gallery r35 repaints the west-wall river procession to add Rei-chan beside the Otani duck, Urata and Howkey; the r34 friezes (Saber, Fairy, nukonuko, Saga; duck, Urata, Howkey) replaced the lone deer and bison. The original GLB is unchanged.",
    "Gallery r36 uses eight equally scaled 7.5 m processions, eighteen additional upper animal paintings and four hand/sign motifs. Coming Soon is removed. Pigment follows inward limestone folds. Per-character animal replacement recipes preserve visible neighbours and avoid runtime texture additions."
  ],
